@Archit3ch (George) Oh, also: please try to replicate your testbench behavior on IHP SG13 (G2 or CMOS5L variant shouldn't matter to demonstrate base function, I think, as this shouldn't require dnwell to work/exist as a concept), because that uses different mosfet models (PSP 103 instead of BSIM4) which AFAIK put waaaay more emphasis on charge conservation.

The working idea behind it is that the positive charge on the gate poly sucks the interesting/signal-coding negative charge in the trench below along, if you use at least 3 clock phases that overlap and that each have less than 50% duty cycle.
Assuming n-channel operation; reverse polarities if it'd be p-channel operation instead. I don't know which of the two carriers would realistically exhibit longer useful lifetime here, though.
